    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d920">

                <pb facs="0835" n="719" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg719"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/2771.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of War to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">War Department</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 12, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Following telegram * * * from commanding general central division dated Chicago,
                    Ill., February 11, 1912, repeated for your information: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Steever wires to department headquarters, 10th: “Turned Mexican
                            prisoners, captured Noria, over to proper civil authorities. Retained
                            arms and mounts at request Mexican consul, who claims belong to his
                            Government. Recommend they be delivered to him. * * *”</p>
                        <p rendition="#right">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Potts</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Commanding</hi>.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry L. Stimson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
